IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `bk63-nouns`

-- Row il-63. THE ONE ITEM (I1), as typed values, with sound controls beside it.
-- A reference is encoded as TWO descriptions: what the citing words say they point at, and what the target is, with a count of what is named and what the target has. Where they differ, the citation does not point at what it says.
-- DEFECT I1: s 5ב(א) of the Law says that financial activity is as defined in s 5ב1(ה); the definition stands in s 5ב1(א), and s 5ב1(ה) holds a power of the Governor. Its failing assertions are in bk63-tests-xrefs-red.l4.
-- CONTROLS: (1) a second reference to the same subsection (ה), in s 3 of the Act in Sefer HaChukim 3510, whose target holds what the words say; (2) the words that the Act in Sefer HaChukim 2712 inserted into s 5ב(א) and the words the consolidation prints at that place, which are the same.
-- LIMBS. Limb (a) is the question whether the target is as the citing words say; limb (b) is the question whether the citing words read so in the instrument that made them.
-- Each limb says where it was read from (see `Where a reading comes from` in bk63-nouns.l4). The Hebrew Wikisource text is not official, and anything resting only on it is CONSOLIDATION-ONLY.
-- This row records one reference. It does not say that the Law or anyone is wrong, and it does not say what a court would do with the words.

§ `The subsections that the references name and point at`

-- The target of the defect: subsection (ה) of s 5ב1. The words are on the page of the Act in Sefer HaChukim 2712 that is printed 455 (read from the deposited cropped image: the crop holds the subsection and the footer line, in bands, and nothing else of the page):
-- ext:[SH 2712 p.455, read from the deposited cropped image] | (ה) הנגיד, בהסכמת שר האוצר, רשאי לקבוע, משיקולים הנוגעים לעלות הכרוכה ביישום הוראות סעיף זה או לתחרות במערכת הבנקאית, לבקשתו של בנק בעל היקף פעילות קטן או בנק מקוון, כי הוראות סעיף זה לא יחולו עליו, יחולו עליו בתום תקופה שיקבע הנגיד, או שיחולו עליו חובות רק כבנק קולט או כבנק מקורי.
-- The consolidation has the same subsection (CONSOLIDATION-ONLY); its bank kinds differ from the 2018 page (it names three kinds of bank, the 2018 page two), and the row relies on neither list:
